D) from in vitro reactions after <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradiene was reacted with the cell-free lysates analyzed in (A) or (C), respectively (peak 1, <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradiene; peak 2, <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradien-19-ol; peak 3, <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradien-19-al; peak 4 methyl ester derivative of <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradien-19-oic acid). E, Reaction catalyzed by CYP99A2 (compounds numbered corresponding to peak labels defined above).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" position=\"float\" orientation=\"portrait\" xlink:href=\"nihms-671238-f0001.jpg\"/></fig><fig id=\"F2\" orientation=\"portrait\" position=\"float\"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>CYP701A8 catalytic activity. A, GC-MS selected ion (<italic toggle=\"yes\">m/z</italic> = 272 + 288) chromatogram of extract from <italic toggle=\"yes\">E. coli</italic> engineered for production of <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradiene with co-expression of CYP99A2 and AtCPR1 (peak 1, <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradiene; peak 2: <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradien-3β-ol). B, Mass spectrum for <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradien-3β-ol. C, Reaction catalyzed by CYP701A8 with <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradiene.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" position=\"float\" orientation=\"portrait\" xlink:href=\"nihms-671238-f0002.jpg\"/></fig><fig id=\"F3\" orientation=\"portrait\" position=\"float\"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>CYP71Z6 and CYP71Z7 catalytic activities. A &amp; D, GC-MS chromatograms of cell-free lysate from <italic toggle=\"yes\">E. coli</italic> engineered for production of either (A) <italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-cassadiene with co-expression of CYP71Z7 and AtCPR1 (peak 1, <italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-cassadiene; peak 2, <italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-cassadien-2-one; peak 3; 2α-hydroxy-<italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-cassadiene, peak 4, 3α-hydroxy-<italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-cassadien-2-one), or (D) <italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-isokaurene with co-expression of CYP71Z6 and AtCPR1 (peak 5, <italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-isokaurene; peak 6, 2α-hydroxy-<italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-isokaurene; peak 7, 2α,3α-dihydroxy-<italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-isokaurene). B, C &amp; E, Mass spectra from (B) <italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-cassadien-2-one, (C) 3α-hydroxy-<italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-cassadien-2-one, or (E) 2α,3α-dihydroxy-<italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-isokaurene. F, Reactions catalyzed by CYP71Z6 &amp; CYP71Z7 (as indicated).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" position=\"float\" orientation=\"portrait\" xlink:href=\"nihms-671238-f0003.jpg\"/></fig><fig id=\"F4\" orientation=\"portrait\" position=\"float\"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Putative roles for CYP activities reported here in rice diterpenoid biosynthesis. A, Difference in configurations of ‘A’ rings from <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>- or <italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>-CPP derived diterpenes, with regards to hydrogen targeted by CYP701A8 (note that the <italic toggle=\"yes\">ent</italic>- ‘A’ ring has been “flipped over” relative to the standard orientation, and the <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>- ‘A’ ring). B, Three CYP activities against <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradiene targeting all three oxygenated positions common to the momilactones. C, Putative role of CYP71Z6 in production of oryzadione and related fatty acid ester derivative. D, Role of CYP71Z7 in phytocassane biosynthetic network.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" position=\"float\" orientation=\"portrait\" xlink:href=\"nihms-671238-f0004.jpg\"/></fig><table-wrap id=\"T1\" position=\"float\" orientation=\"portrait\"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Steady-state kinetic constants against <italic toggle=\"yes\">syn</italic>-pimaradiene.</p></caption><table frame=\"hsides\" rules=\"groups\"><thead><tr><th align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">enzyme</th><th align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">K<sub>m</sub> (μM)</th><th align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">k<sub>cat</sub> (s-<sup>1</sup>)</th><th align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">k<sub>cat</sub>/K<sub>M</sub> (s-<sup>1</sup>μM-<sup>1</sup>)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">CYP76M8<xref ref-type=\"table-fn\" rid=\"TFN1\">*</xref><sup><xref ref-type=\"table-fn\" rid=\"TFN2\">1</xref></sup></td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">4 ± 2</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">9.0 ± 1.0 (× 10<sup>−3</sup>)</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">2.3 × 10<sup>−3</sup></td></tr><tr><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">CYP99A2</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">1.2 ± 0.1</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">8.3 ± 0.1</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">7.0</td></tr><tr><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">CYP99A3<xref ref-type=\"table-fn\" rid=\"TFN1\">*</xref><sup><xref ref-type=\"table-fn\" rid=\"TFN3\">2</xref></sup></td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">2.0 ± 0.5</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">46 ± 2</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">23</td></tr><tr><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">CYP701A8</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">27 ± 6</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">1.4 ± 0.1</td><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" rowspan=\"1\" colspan=\"1\">5.2 × 10<sup>−2</sup></td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id=\"TFN1\"><label>*</label><p id=\"P40\">Data from previous reports</p></fn><fn id=\"TFN2\"><label>1</label><p id=\"P41\">(Wang et al. 2012a)</p></fn><fn id=\"TFN3\"><label>2</label><p id=\"P42\">(Wang et al. 2011).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article></pmc-articleset>", "source": "PMC:PMC4546517", "error": ""}
