ef=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nuccore/EcMPOBMT\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">\n<italic toggle=\"yes\">Ec</italic>MPOBMT</ext-link>, <ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nuccore/OP382847\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">OP382847</ext-link>; <ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nuccore/EcCYP81AN15\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">\n<italic toggle=\"yes\">Ec</italic>CYP81AN15</ext-link>, <ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nuccore/OP382848\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">OP382848</ext-link>. The custom R scripts used for hierarchical clustering analysis of Erythroxylaceae transcriptome datasets will be available at the time of publication on the Smolke Laboratory GitHub repository (<ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"https://github.com/smolkelab/coca_coexpression_analysis\" ext-link-type=\"uri\">https://github.com/smolkelab/coca_coexpression_analysis</ext-link>).</p></sec><ref-list><ref id=\"r1\"><label>1</label><mixed-citation publication-type=\"journal\"><person-group person-group-type=\"author\"><string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>J.</given-names>\n<surname>Jirschitzka</surname></string-name>\n<etal/></person-group>, <article-title>Plant tropane alkaloid biosynthesis evolved independently in the Solanaceae and Erythroxylaceae</article-title>. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U.S.A.</source>\n<volume><bold>109</bold></volume>, <fpage>10304</fpage>–<lpage>10309</lpage> (<year>2012</year>).<pub-id pub-id-type=\"pmid\">22665766</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type=\"doi\" assigning-authority=\"pmc\">10.1073/pnas.1200473109</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type=\"pmcid\">PMC3387132</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id=\"r2\"><label>2</label><mixed-citation publication-type=\"book\"><person-group person-group-type=\"author\"><string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>M.</given-names>\n<surname>Lounasmaa</surname></string-name>, <string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>T.</given-names>\n<surname>Tamminen</surname></string-name></person-group>, “<article-title>The tropane alkaloids</article-title>” in <source>The Alkaloids: Chemistry and Pharmacology</source>, <person-group person-group-type=\"author\"><string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>G. A.</given-names>\n<surname>Cordell</surname></string-name></person-group>, <role>Ed.</role> (<publisher-name>Academic Press</publisher-name>, <year>1993</year>), pp. <fpage>1</fpage>–<lpage>114</lpage>.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id=\"r3\"><label>3</label><mixed-citation publication-type=\"journal\"><person-group person-group-type=\"author\"><string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>P.-A.</given-names>\n<surname>Nocquet</surname></string-name>, <string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>T.</given-names>\n<surname>Opatz</surname></string-name></person-group>, <article-title>Total synthesis of (±)-scopolamine: challenges of the tropane ring</article-title>. <source>Eur. J. Org. Chem.</source>\n<volume><bold>2016</bold></volume>, <fpage>1156</fpage>–<lpage>1164</lpage> (<year>2016</year>).</mixed-citation></ref><ref id=\"r4\"><label>4</label><mixed-citation publication-type=\"journal\"><person-group person-group-type=\"author\"><string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>P. C.</given-names>\n<surname>Meltzer</surname></string-name>, <string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>Y.</given-names>\n<surname>Anna</surname></string-name>, <string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>Bertha</given-names>\n<surname>Liang</surname></string-name>, <string-name name-style=\"western\"><given-names>K.</given-names>\n<surname>Madras</surname></string-name></person-group>, <article-title>The discovery of an unusually selective and novel cocaine analog: Difluoropine. Synthesis and inhibition of binding at cocaine recognition sites</article-title>. <source>J. Med. Chem.</source>\n<volume><bold>